# ===========================================================================
# This repository is public, and the thing it is trying not to leak is always
# the file nobody thought of.
#
# Four separate leaks were caught by hand while preparing the first commit: a
# production server's IP address and a *second person's* username in an
# internal runbook; a personal Downloads path inside local tool config; a
# hardcoded home directory in an obsolete launchd plist; and 2.5 GB of database
# snapshots containing real push-subscriber endpoints. Every one of them was
# found by a human squinting at a file list — none by a rule written in
# advance, because each rule was written *after* the near-miss it describes.
#
# So the rules below are deliberately about **categories** rather than about
# the specific files that have burned us. A key, a database, a dump or a log is
# ignored wherever it appears in the tree, not only where one happens to live
# today. Adding a directory should never silently add a secret to it.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Anywhere in the tree, not just data/secrets/. A key committed once is
# compromised permanently: deleting the commit does not un-publish it, and for
# the VAPID key specifically, rotating it invalidates every existing push
# subscription. Nothing here is worth a "just this once".
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
**/secrets/
*credentials*.json
*.secret

# --- The archive itself ----------------------------------------------------
# Everything under data/ is runtime state. Deny-by-default, not a list of
# known-bad paths: the earlier list version enumerated tenders.db, docs/,
# html/ and captcha/ and silently missed data/backups/ — full database copies,
# push_subscriptions table included, staged and ready to push. Enumerating what
# to hide fails the moment a new subdirectory appears; enumerating what to keep
# fails safe instead.
#
# Nothing in data/ belongs in git: config.ensure_dirs() recreates the tree and
# the archive is rebuilt by scraping. If something in here ever does need
# tracking, add a targeted `!data/thing` exception and say why.
data/

# Databases and their sidecars, wherever they turn up. A WAL and a shm are as
# disclosing as the .db they belong to, and a mid-write copy of any of the
# three is also corrupt — see docs/SELF-HOSTING.md on backups.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.sql.zst

# Captured documents, archived HTML, generated share cards.
*.tar.zst
*.tar.gz
og/

# --- Logs ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs quote URLs, tender ids, filesystem paths and occasionally a stack trace
# with local variables in it. None of that is interesting enough to publish and
# some of it is machine-identifying.
*.log
logs/

# --- Machine-specific and operator-specific --------------------------------
# ARCHITECTURE.md documents *this installation*: the production server's IP
# address, home-directory paths, the hostname, the uid the units run under, and
# the username of a second person on the wider cluster. None of it helps anyone
# self-host, and one of the names in it is not ours to publish. The public
# equivalents are README.md and docs/SELF-HOSTING.md, which describe the system
# without describing the machine. If a design-rationale doc is ever wanted in
# the repo, write it fresh — a redaction pass over a runbook is exactly the
# kind of thing that misses a line.
ARCHITECTURE.md

# Local tool config. Anything named *.local.* was never meant to be shared, and
# these files accumulate absolute paths from whatever machine touched them.
.claude/
*.local.json
*.local.toml
*.local.yml

# Obsolete macOS launchd agent with a hardcoded home directory baked in.
# Superseded by deploy/*.service, which use systemd's %h and therefore work for
# whoever installs them.
scripts/com.tenders.forward.plist

# --- Editors and operating systems -----------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Models and training artefacts -----------------------------------------
# The trained captcha model is reproducible (see the README's cold start) and
# a checkpoint is tens of megabytes of binary that git cannot diff. It lives in
# data/ and is caught above; these catch a stray copy elsewhere.
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.ckpt

# --- Scratch ---------------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
tmp/
scratch/
